## Summary

Shipped a production-polished, native Apple (SwiftUI) **`BatteryGaugeWidget`** at full parity with `web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/BatteryGaugeWidget.tsx`, as 7 files in the allowed scope (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/BatteryGaugeWidget.*`) — 1,574 lines, committed as `9d83abeb7`.

**Parity reproduced from the web source:**
- Data via the shared P1/S8 `BatteryGaugeWidgetSource` seam (`useVehicles` + `useVehicleState`) — no HTTP in the view.
- `batteryColor` bands verbatim: >50 green `#10b981`, >20 amber `#f59e0b`, else red `#ef4444` (+ `#374151` neutral).
- Radial gauge readout `fmtNumber(clamped 0..100, integer→0/else precision)` + `%`, "Battery" caption, and the `⚡ Charging` caption (gated on `is_charging` + `!compact`).
- Every state renders: loading / empty ("No battery data") / error+retry / stale / offline / content.
- Registry `battery-gauge`, category `battery`, sizes 1×2 / 1×2 / 2×40 (clamp enforced).
- All i18n through the P1/S10 facade (no English literals), VoiceOver labels + Dynamic Type + Reduce-Motion, and the `view.opened` (P1/S11) telemetry with slug `BatteryGaugeWidget`.

